Enhancement: Make index checks memory-first and quota-aware

`vaultic index check` now defaults `--check-memory` to `auto`, deriving a
checker-buffer budget from available host and cgroup memory while preserving
headroom for the operating system and reclaimable file cache. Explicit byte
values continue to provide fixed admission budgets.

Location and key/value checker spools retain sorted runs in memory while they
fit, then use authenticated encrypted scratch on overflow. Direct tuple
comparison and fixed-capacity memory runs reduce synthetic checker time,
allocation volume, and peak RSS without changing exact comparison results.

